    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "IRDAI was established following the recommendations of the Malhotra Committee report in 1999.",
        "SEBI acquired statutory status through the SEBI Act, 1992, giving it enforcement powers over capital markets.",
        "RBI was nationalized on January 1, 1949, under the Reserve Bank (Transfer to Public Ownership) Act."
      ],
      "id": "4t3bwlr"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "RBI is the apex monetary authority regulating banks, money markets, and foreign exchange in India.",
        "SEBI regulates the securities and capital markets to protect investor interests and ensure market integrity.",
        "IRDAI oversees the insurance and re-insurance industries to promote fair trade and protect policyholders.",
        "While RBI and SEBI are headquartered in Mumbai, IRDAI's headquarters are located in Hyderabad."
      ],
